S - Fusion Axiom

Fusion is the birth of the new from the two. The Substitution / Fusion Axiom distributes an argument across two functions and fuses the results.
S f g x = (f x) (g x).

🌊

@[ts]

// 🔗 Implicit Gravity: No imports required. Dependencies are in the DNA.
export const S = <A, B, C>(f: (x: A) => (y: B) => C) => (g: (x: A) => B) => (x: A): C => f(x)(g(x));


@[rs]

// 🔗 Native implementation
pub fn S<A, B, C, F, G>(f: F, g: G, x: A) -> C
where
    F: Fn(A) -> Box<dyn Fn(B) -> C>,
    G: Fn(A) -> B,
    A: Clone,
{
    f(x.clone())(g(x))
}


@[sh]

# 🔗 Shell implementation
S() {
    local f="$1"
    local g="$2"
    local x="$3"
    echo "S-Fusion: ($f $x) ($g $x)"
}


